<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - Dutch unemployment seen little changed.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dutch unemployment seen little changed.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch economists expect unemployment figures for December-February due on Wednesday to be little changed compared with November-January.</p>
<p>They forecast a small rise in the non-seasonally adjusted unemployment figure, but they expect the seasonally adjusted figure to be somewhat lower.</p>
<p>Economists' forecasts are summarised below.</p>
<p>   GMT---Date--Period---Indicator---------Consensus--Range----Pvs</p>
<p>  0830  19/3  Dec-Feb  Unemployment NSA  438,000    433-442  437</p>
<p>  0830  19/3  Dec-Feb  Unemployment SA   427,000    422-431  429</p>
<p>Forecasts contributed by: ABN AMRO, Generale Bank, ING, J.P. Morgan, MeesPierson, NIB Securities, Rabobank.</p>
<p>-- Christine Lucassen, Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000</p>
